# STM32WLE5 – LoRaWAN IoT Monitoring

## Project Overview

This project was carried out during an engineering internship at **YUCCAINFO**.

The main objective was to study and experiment with an intelligent IoT monitoring node based on the **STM32WLE5** microcontroller and LoRaWAN communication.

The work focused on hardware architecture, LoRaWAN configuration, AT command experiments, and communication with **The Things Network (TTN)** through a Dragino gateway.

## Project Objectives

- Study the STM32WLE5JC microcontroller architecture.
- Explore the LoRa-E5 development board.
- Analyze a custom hardware schematic based on the RAK3172 module.
- Understand LoRaWAN communication and OTAA activation.
- Configure the EU868 frequency plan.
- Test communication with The Things Network.
- Explore MQTT as a future data-monitoring solution.

